  "title": "PoloHortiguela2025: Motor imagery of ankle dorsiflexion/plantarflexion dataset",
  "description": "Open-loop EEG dataset of kinesthetic motor imagery of lower-limb ankle dorsiflexion/plantarflexion alternated with relaxation, recorded from six healthy participants. Each participant completed two sessions, one with a static and one with a motion lower-limb exoskeleton model, using 28 EEG channels plus EOG at 250 Hz. This BIDS re-release was generated with MOABB from the original Zenodo deposit.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded at 250 Hz from 28 EEG channels, 4 EOG channels and 3 auxiliary channels (standard_1005 montage, 50 Hz line frequency). Participants performed cue-based (auditory) kinesthetic motor imagery of ankle dorsiflexion/plantarflexion versus rest in 4 s trials, over 11 runs per session, with a static or a motion exoskeleton.",
